SUMMARY:Scholarly Write-In
DESCRIPTION:Write and work in solidarity with other IU scholars. We offer a 
 silent work environment with coffee and natural light. The write-in is open 
 to all graduate students (at any stage of their degree program).\n\nMeets 
 weekly throughout the semester\, Thursday from 1-3pm. No meeting during 
 spring break.\n\nCo-sponsored by Writing Tutorial Services and the IU 
 Libraries.\n\nDrop in or come weekly as your schedule permits.
LOCATION:Writing Tutorial Services (Wells W110)
ORGANIZER;CN="Alyssa Denneler":MAILTO:alydenn@iu.edu
CATEGORIES:Citing, Writing & Research Tools
UID:LibCal-1228-16225032
URL:https://iub.libcal.com/event/16225032
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260505T131500Z
DTEND:20260505T153000Z
DTSTAMP:20260505T000000Z
SUMMARY:Supercharge Your Dissertation
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a workshop where libraries faculty and campus 
 experts share their insights on how to make the most of your dissertation 
 writing.\n\nWhether you’re just about to start working on your 
 dissertation\, or just need a boost\, we want to set you up to get the most 
 out of the summer months.\n\nBagels and coffee will be served.\n\nThis 
 year's schedule:\n\n\n	Establishing a Daily Writing Practice\n	High Impact 
 Publishing Practices\n	Finding and Using Data\n
LOCATION:Hazelbaker Hall (Wells E159)
ORGANIZER;CN="Reference Desk Staff":MAILTO:libschol@iu.edu
CATEGORIES:Citing, Writing & Research Tools
UID:LibCal-1228-16630304
URL:https://iub.libcal.com/event/16630304
END:VEVENT

